  "topic": "Read and write Seen (س) at the beginning, middle and end of words, with Fatha, Kasra and Damma.",
  "minutes": 10,
  "learn": [
    {
      "en": "This is Seen. Like 's' in 'sun' or 'smile'. A clear, crisp hissing sound. No buzzing!",
      "title": "Meet Seen!",
      "ar": "س",
      "aud": "c-0-ar",
      "tr": "Seen"
    },
    {
      "en": "Three small humps (teeth) on a flat baseline like a mini fence or ocean waves! Seen looks like THREE WAVES on the sea S for Sea, S for Seen!",
      "title": "How to write Seen"
    },
    {
      "en": "With a fatha, Seen says “sa”.",
      "title": "Seen with fatha",
      "ar": "سَ",
      "aud": "c-2-ar"
    },
    {
      "en": "With a kasra, Seen says “se”.",
      "title": "Seen with kasra",
      "ar": "سِ",
      "aud": "c-3-ar"
    },
    {
      "en": "With a damma, Seen says “so”.",
      "title": "Seen with damma",
      "ar": "سُ",
      "aud": "c-4-ar"
    },
    {
      "en": "“The sky is blue”",
      "title": "Sentence of the lesson",
      "ar": "السَّمَاءُ زَرْقَاء",
      "aud": "c-5-ar",
      "tr": "Al-Sama'u Zarqa'"
    }
